# The mesh: every machine, one line each. Everything else in mesh/ that names
# a machine is generated from this by `mesh/build` — mesh.conf, the known
# hosts, the authorized_keys block — and `desktop` reads it at run time.
#
#   name     the short name: `ssh <name>`, `<name>-lan`, `cloudflare-<name>`,
#            `desktop-<name>`; also names hostkeys/<name> and keys/<name>.pub
#   host     its tailnet (MagicDNS) name, which is also `hostname -s` on it;
#            the LAN path is <host>.local
#   user     its login
#   ip       its tailnet address, pinned in known_hosts beside the names
#   tunnel   the hostname its cloudflared carries ssh on, or - for none
#   vnc      the local port `desktop` forwards its screen to over the tunnel;
#            one per machine so several can be open at once
#   github   the account in mesh/accounts it pushes as, or - for none
#   aliases  more names for the tailnet path, and for `desktop`
#
# Comment lines directly above a machine are carried into its section of
# mesh.conf, so a note about one box stays next to that box.
#
# Adding a machine: docs/remote-access.md, "Adding a machine".

# name       host                 user         ip              tunnel                             vnc   github       aliases
